From aee1644f50fd6ba847e2343913f701258bac15af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Berger <dbgh@knownhosts.org>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:37:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(engine): Let a host choose the settlement policy
 (no-changelog)

`createEngineRuntime` built its `StepSettledHandler` without a policy, so
the handler always used `defaultSettlementPolicy`. It now takes an optional
`settlementPolicy` and hands the handler `settlementPolicy ??
getSettlementPolicy()`.

`settlement-policy-registry.ts` holds the process-wide policy:
`setSettlementPolicy()`, `getSettlementPolicy()` and
`resetSettlementPolicy()`. Its default is `defaultSettlementPolicy`. A host
can register a policy without changing a composition root: the in-process
module, the `n8n engine` command and `serve.ts` all build their engine
through `createEngineRuntime`.

The registry is read only in `createEngineRuntime`, once per runtime. It is
not the handler's constructor default, so a handler built directly, as the
handler tests build it, keeps `defaultSettlementPolicy`.

Nothing registers a policy and no caller passes one, so the behaviour does
not change. The existing tests are not edited. Four cases in
`create-engine-runtime.test.ts` check that the handler gets the default
while nothing is registered, the option, the registered policy, and the
option over the registered policy.
